            <ArticleTitle>Surgical one-stage approach for coronary artery disease and occlusive disease of all aortic arch branches.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>293-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 52-year-old man, who presented with two-vessel coronary artery disease and severe arterial occlusive disease with occlusions and/or stenoses of all aortic arch branches, underwent simultaneously coronary artery bypass grafting and bilateral aortic-subclavian as well as left-sided aortic-carotidal bypass grafting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
